  * Apache License, Version 2.0 — see licenses/LICENSE-APACHE
  * MIT license                 — see licenses/LICENSE-MIT

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution intentionally submitted
for inclusion in this project by you shall be dual licensed as above, without any
additional terms or conditions.

This file is a summary. The two files it points at hold the actual licence
texts; if they ever disagree with this summary, they win.

That dual licence covers the repository's own content and nothing else: the
scripts and their tests, the documentation, the Noctua Iosevka build plan
(noctua-iosevka/private-build-plans.toml), and the source of the GitHub Pages
site together with the pages generated from it.

The fonts are NOT covered by it. Every font file here (*.ttf, *.woff2) stays
under the licence of its own family, shipped beside it in its folder's
licenses/ directory. Those terms apply to those files rather than to this
project, and each of them requires its text to travel with the fonts.

  * Noctua Iosevka (noctua-iosevka/), a custom build of Iosevka by Renzhi Li
    — SIL Open Font License 1.1, in noctua-iosevka/licenses/OFL-Iosevka.txt.

  * Noctua Noto (noctua-noto/), the Noto families — SIL Open Font License
    1.1, one licence file per family in noctua-noto/licenses/.

  * Symbols Nerd Font (symbols-nerd-font/), and the Nerd Fonts icons inside
    the patched faces — the Nerd Font builds of Noctua Iosevka and of Noto.
    The Nerd Fonts project ships them with its MIT license, kept in
    symbols-nerd-font/licenses/LICENSE-NerdFontsSymbolsOnly.txt and, byte
    for byte, in noctua-iosevka/licenses/ and noctua-noto/licenses/.
    The icon sets that Nerd Fonts gathers keep their own upstream licences,
    and not all of them are MIT: Codicons and Font Awesome are under CC BY
    4.0, Material Design Icons under Apache 2.0, Pomicons and Weather Icons
    under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and Font Logos under the Unlicense.
    The Nerd Fonts repository, https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts,
    lists every set with its source and licence in license-audit.md and in
    src/glyphs/README.md. The rest of each patched face stays under its
    family's OFL.

The release archives carry the licence files kept here: an archive holds,
beside its fonts, the licence of every family those fonts come from, and the
Nerd Fonts MIT license whenever it holds a Nerd Fonts face. Nerd Fonts' own
Symbols Only release does the same: that MIT file is its only licence text.
No archive carries a separate text for each icon set; for those terms, see
the Nerd Fonts lists named above.
